From 6e60cdb0ed0a2c1769dde871037fc8fb7b9d31e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: friedger <mail@friedger.de>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 13:48:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(belfry): self-custody, take over the key or move to a
 key of one's own

Decisions of 2026-10-24: participants can hold their own Nostr key.

- GET /api/user/self-custody/challenge: a stateless challenge (HMAC with
  the server key) bound to the account, valid ten minutes.
- POST /api/user/self-custody {event}: a kind-27235 event carrying the
  challenge, after a fresh sign-in (OIDC_REAUTH_WINDOW_SECS, like the key
  export). Signed by the account's own key: Keycast deletes its copy and
  every app authorization. Signed by another key: the account moves to it
  (new users row with username, e-mail, vine_id and status; the
  oidc_identities link moves; the old row is orphaned) and the old key and
  authorizations are deleted; the session cookie is cleared.
  With BELFRY_KEY_CHANGED_URL and BELFRY_HOOK_TOKEN Keycast tells the
  onboarding service (pass npub, relay whitelist).
- /api/oauth/authorize: an account without a key held by Keycast gets
  access_denied (error_description self_custody) for prompt=none and a
  branded "Use your own signer" page otherwise.
- GET /api/user/account: key_held. Security page: "Hold your own key"
  (sign the challenge with a browser extension or a pasted key that stays
  in the browser); export only while Keycast holds the key; upstream's
  custodial "Change Private Key" only for password accounts.
